PaMaL demonstrates commendable performance. However, it only focuses on two or three tasks. When dealing with a large number of tasks, the number of parameters increases significantly as each task i requires its own network θi. Moreover, the base networks cannot benefit from each other during training, which can potentially impair performance, especially when scaling to a larger number of base networks.
Learning a continuous PF is also explored in Bayesian optimization (Lin et al., 2022b) and evolutionary optimization (Lin et al., 2023) for engineering problems with number of parameters up to 7. They fail to converge in deep learning scenarios due to the significantly larger parameter spaces.
2.3. Low-Rank Adaptation
Low-rank adaptation (LoRA) has emerged as a popular approach in the field of finetuning large pre-trained models
